  "details": "Example avatar:\navtr_d87d4acc-f058-432b-aa1c-373b6fcb3e6d\nThe expression menu enables/disables the cube, and right hand grip uses a normalized time state to rotate the cube.  However, once the normalized time state is transitioned to, the cube can never be disabled by the menu even though the AV3 debug menu says all parameters and states are correct.\n\nUPDATE: 1D blendtrees driven by GestureRightWeight/GestureLeftWeight succumb to the same problem.  Example avatar:\navtr_c83df5f9-e48e-4bb7-926d-aaf3dae490d8\n\nUPDATE 2: Apparently this is a Unity bug, and the only mitigation to make normalized time states and blendtrees work is to have them on a layer ABOVE the layer that is enabling/disabling gameobjects.",
